Z||000000||Blondie88||10-23-2001||05:11 PM||||Hi!  I'm moving to calgary in 4 months and I was wondering if anyone knew anything about the job market there or living situations.  I'm gonna be an immigrant *gasp* but hopefully it'll go alright.  Any information anyone has would be great!  Thanks muchos.  Surprisingly the internet can only do so much! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||10-23-2001||06:15 PM||||heheheh..... Calgary  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>3 things:<P>1) Watch yourself on the roads. Calgarians can be NASTY<BR>2) Housing tends to be nice, if a little pricey... Most of the available housing is in new development areas. The hardest part is navigating through a psuedo-grid system. Kinda like the grid system, only with "regular" street name and direction conventions. A real PITA until you get used to it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>3) No idea on job market. Calgary is still growing fast, so I'd assume that there's plenty around, if you look. Regardless, no-one will ever make an issue of you being an immigrant, except maybe to take you out for some REAL beer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Oh, and practice on your "Eh," Eh?<P><BR>Good luck!||||reg||10
Z||000002||fierobaby||10-23-2001||06:18 PM||||EH!? (couldn't resist!)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neal||10-23-2001||07:36 PM||||What you saying about calgary drivers being nasty...<BR>Hmmm never had a problem with driving (other than the usual sh!t) but who knows<P>Job market is great, i dont know what your looking for but most industries are hireing<P>Yes housing is in demand and expensive.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||10-23-2001||08:38 PM||||3 words: TRANS CANADA EAST<BR>I've learned to DREAD that Alberta license plate on the ON-ramps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>In the city they aren't that bad... The layout STILL sucks   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000005||FLASHY||10-23-2001||11:02 PM||||Great economy, VERY fast growing, traffic isn't usually bad but can be (nothing like Miami or China  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) It takes very little time to get used to the roads in my opinion. It's a city I don't feel like moving away from. Looking forward to meeting you at our club some day. Let us know when you make it here. Here's our club webpage...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/</A> <P>*<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spinsig3.gif"> ||||reg||14
