Z||000008||Brandon86SE||10-24-2001||04:30 AM||||hurrah for Calgary!  I just moved here a year ago, and it's great!  By far the best place I've ever lived.  Also, we have an amazing, and really active Fiero club.  You'll love it!  (oh, and the driving isn't bad at all)<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Voytek||10-24-2001||02:29 PM||||I think Blondie88 has left the building...<P>Nonetheless, if you're still reading the responses, Calgary is a really good place to live if you don't mind the winters.  We got about 2-3 inches of snow last night with a temperature of about 29 deg F.<P>The job market CAN be good - all depends on what you're looking for.  Plenty of 'help wanted' signs on gas stations and convenience stores.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I've driven through Nevada in August.  MAN, what a HOT place.  This will definitely be a change for ya.<P>I work with 2 guys from Texas.  One loves it here - the other one hates the weather.<P>Hopefully we'll see you at the club in the spring (I believe it's over for this season).<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Blondie88||10-24-2001||03:56 PM||||Hey! I haven't left the building just yet.  Thanks for all the info.  I've been to calgary a few times, my boyfriend lives outside carseland.  I think i'll fit right in with Alberta drivers! I'm not exactly sane behind the wheel...but i try!<P>As for the housing, my limit (if I dont have a roommate) is about 600 canadian/month.  I think I can live with that kind of rent for a couple months living off of my "american income" psh. but i'll need a job quick.  I'm looking into being a secretary, but i'm damn good at pumping gas too!  So I'd do that if it'd keep me alive!  haha hmmm <P>Don't have a fiero yet, but i'm sure i'll have one soon...maybe in a couple years.  I'd still love to meet you all, i'll probably be coming to the spring meetings with my boyfriend and his 86 GT. <P>Thanks again and yes Nevada is really hot.  We're all still in shorts and t-shirts! i'll see you on the roads in february!  If I get good tires for christmas... =0) ||||reg||1
Z||000011||RiceCooker||10-25-2001||02:38 PM||||Yup, lookin forward to seein ya in the springtime. Voytek's right about the job market, it all depends on what your lookin for. <BR>Also gonna take this opportunity to say bye bye to my car for the year. I almost made it (199,700km) take it easy CALGARIANS<P>...and blondie, i can show you where the good casinos are  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000012||Blondie88||10-25-2001||02:44 PM||||Ya know, I think me and casinos don't mix.  Maybe it's all the smoke or the fact that I always lose all my money!  hahaha i'd play poker for a little bit...Texas hold 'em is my favorite, we play it at home a lot.  It's so weird that i'll be LEGAL in canada!  haha hmmm but yeah, i'll definitely be wanting some people to show me around and get used to the city!  Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
